**Convention 2.5 (observation and access).** The theorem compares actual
row-successor observations, not an original hidden-query trace. Actor $A$
already owns the active banks and the source seal; the scan uses only
that current authority. The mathematical inverse is not an extra native
operation or a uniform actor procedure choosing a stopping time. It makes
no original-$Q$ claim until the interface conditions of §5 hold. In
particular it is different from EXPOSURE's 010/100 payload exposure: here
an arbitrary completed predecessor, rather than one bit of a pending
history frame, is recovered before the next header input.

